1	//! Bivvy - Interactive development environment setup automation.
2	//!
3	//! Bivvy is a CLI tool that replaces ad-hoc `bin/setup` scripts with
4	//! declarative YAML configuration and a polished interactive CLI experience.
5	//!
6	//! # Modules
7	//!
8	//! - [`cli`] - Command-line interface and argument parsing
9	//! - [`config`] - Configuration loading, parsing, and validation
10	//! - [`environment`] - Environment detection and resolution
11	//! - [`error`] - Error types and result aliases
12	//! - [`lint`] - Configuration validation and linting
13	//! - [`logging`] - Structured event logging (JSONL)
14	//! - [`registry`] - Template registry and resolution
15	//! - [`runner`] - Step execution orchestration and dependency management
16	//! - [`shell`] - Shell command execution
17	//! - [`state`] - State management for execution history and preferences
18	//! - [`secrets`] - Secret detection and output masking
19	//! - [`steps`] - Step resolution and execution
20	//! - [`ui`] - Interactive prompts, spinners, and terminal output
21	//!
22	//! # Example
23	//!
24	//! ```
25	//! use bivvy::config::{InterpolationContext, resolve_string};
26	//!
27	//! // Resolve variables in a command
28	//! let mut ctx = InterpolationContext::new();
29	//! ctx.prompts.insert("mode".to_string(), "development".to_string());
30	//! let command = resolve_string("rails s -e ${mode}", &ctx).unwrap();
31	//! assert_eq!(command, "rails s -e development");
32	//! ```
33	//!
34	//! For file-based config loading, see the integration tests.
35	
